# Our nexus — deployment config

This is the **our-cloud side of THE LINE**: the runtime ships neutral, and *our* values live here, as
config. It's the `deployment.work` our control-plane nexus reads through `Nexus.Config` (a `deploy`
block, never env vars, never constants in `lib/`). Dogfooding: we run our own nexus the exact way we
ask everyone else to — a `.work` config declaration, read at boot.

At deploy this file is placed where `Nexus.Config` looks (`/data/deployment.work`); here it is the
tracked source of truth. Secrets are NOT here — those come through `Nexus.Secrets` from the encrypted
control-plane store; this is only tunable config + our public business values.

deploy do
  # Our capacity tiers — the numbers the dashboard + the upsell read. `id | Name | ram_mb storage_gb price_usd domains(yes|no)`.
  tiers="
    starter | Starter | 1024 10 0 no
    team    | Team    | 4096 100 49 yes
    scale   | Scale   | 16384 1000 199 yes
  "

  reserved-hosts="workbooks.sh"                          # our domain of record — tenants can't bind under it
  runtime-image="ghcr.io/workbooks-sh/runtime:latest"   # the image we provision per-tenant

  search="brave"                                         # cloud web-search: keyed Brave (reliable from datacenter IPs)
  compile-cache="on"
end
